The SSE specification (W3C section 6) requires parsers to handle all three line ending styles: LF (
), CR LF (
), and bare CR (). The parser at line 72 only splits on '
'. While most modern servers use LF, a 
 response will leave trailing  characters on each line, causing field parsing to fail (e.g., 'event:update' would set eventType to 'update' instead of 'update'). Bare  line endings would not split at all, causing the entire stream to be treated as one long incomplete line.

